From 761af9d196ec7529da57401eb97c0ceaac35d6de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:55:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] rtc_base: back physical sockets with AROSTCP [chromium]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: WebRTC's physical socket server called libc socket APIs directly and treated every POSIX target as Linux for receive timestamps, ancillary ECN metadata, PMTU discovery, and receive-traffic-class options. AROS sockets require per-task bsdsocket.library calls and do not expose those Linux capabilities.

FIX_REASON: Route each core socket operation through explicit local RTC_OS adapters backed by Chromium's AROSTCP service, use its nonblocking transition, and mark unsupported timestamp/ancillary receive-ECN/PMTU options unavailable instead of inventing constants or metadata.

SCOPE: rtc_base/physical_socket_server.cc and the threading target's //base dependency.

VALIDATION: focused physical_socket_server.o compiles after the full graph reached this target; async DNS and QUIC libraries had already completed.

RISK: medium; socket operations are native, but the POSIX pipe/select wakeup path still requires runtime validation against AROS event integration.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
